(6447341, 940296, 123833, '<td valign="top">I think this is by far your best challenge entry and could get published on 1x. Your current profile page mostly represents the preference of a mythical average DPCer and would be unlikely to be published on 1x. Am I right? What do you think? I am interested in understanding what 1x selectors select and why certain images are very successful on DPC but do not get published on 1x.</td>', 'I think this is by far your best challenge entry and could get published on 1x. Your current profile page mostly represents the preference of a mythical average DPCer and would be unlikely to be published on 1x. Am I right? What do you think? I am interested in understanding what 1x selectors select and why certain images are very successful on DPC but do not get published on 1x.', '2011-06-19 13:31:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(6447374, 940296, 112972, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by MargaretN:</b></div><hr/><i> I think this is by far your best challenge entry and could get published on 1x. Your current profile page mostly represents the preference of a mythical average DPCer and would be unlikely to be published on 1x. Am I right? What do you think? I am interested in understanding what 1x selectors select and why certain images are very successful on DPC but do not get published on 1x. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>You probably know more about 1x than I do.  If you think this might do well over there, I might try uploading it and see how it will received.  I wouldn''t care one way or the other.  1x.com isn''t a site I hang out regularly.  Besides why should I care what style 1x.com likes?  I am not going to alter my style just so that it becomes less DPC-like and more 1x.com like.  I put a lot more stock into DPC than 1x because it involves a much larger sample size than it does on 1x which is basically what 1 single curator thinks of the images submitted over there.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2012-02-04 20:02:41.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by MargaretN: I think this is by far your best challenge entry and could get published on 1x. Your current profile page mostly represents the preference of a mythical average DPCer and would be unlikely to be published on 1x. Am I right? What do you think? I am interested in understanding what 1x selectors select and why certain images are very successful on DPC but do not get published on 1x.   You probably know more about 1x than I do.  If you think this might do well over there, I might try uploading it and see how it will received.  I wouldn''t care one way or the other.  1x.com isn''t a site I hang out regularly.  Besides why should I care what style 1x.com likes?  I am not going to alter my style just so that it becomes less DPC-like and more 1x.com like.  I put a lot more stock into DPC than 1x because it involves a much larger sample size than it does on 1x which is basically what 1 single curator thinks of the images submitted over there.', '2011-06-19 15:03:37.000000', '2012-02-04 20:02:41.000000', 0),
(6449618, 940296, 41337, '<td valign="top">"This image is special to me because it won both the Posthumous Blue and the usual blue. First time that this has ever happened on DPC."<br/> <br/>Actually the first time was in 2007 in Still Life With Motion challenge. ;)</td>', '"This image is special to me because it won both the Posthumous Blue and the usual blue. First time that this has ever happened on DPC." Actually the first time was in 2007 in Still Life With Motion challenge. ;)', '2011-06-21 22:05:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(6449691, 940296, 112972, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by yanko:</b></div><hr/><i> "This image is special to me because it won both the Posthumous Blue and the usual blue. First time that this has ever happened on DPC."<br/> <br/>Actually the first time was in 2007 in Still Life With Motion challenge. ;) </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thank you for the correction!  Posthumous and I looked and looked but couldn''t find another one.  Congrats to you on being the 1st!</td>', 'Originally posted by yanko: "This image is special to me because it won both the Posthumous Blue and the usual blue. First time that this has ever happened on DPC." Actually the first time was in 2007 in Still Life With Motion challenge. ;)   Thank you for the correction!  Posthumous and I looked and looked but couldn''t find another one.  Congrats to you on being the 1st!', '2011-06-21 22:54:14.000000', NULL, 0),
